      "value": "@{5c1419f79358e0212d61c456|full_name}: Actually, large open worlds can be made highly performant if the worldmaker knows what the hell they are doing. if you want good performance then you ***HAVE*** to have render occlusion, bake your lighting or keep dynamic lighting to a minimum and use LODs. Not to mention just like with avatars, keep the mesh renderers, materials, textures, shaders, and tessellation minimised as much as you possibly can.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
